import Scry.ProveCmd
/-!
# scry-prove: the `scry prove` command without the native parser

The prover corpus and the Lean groups read checked-in `scry-cst` spills, so they need no
tree-sitter and no .NET. The full `scry` CLI links the native parser for its other
commands, which a fresh worktree cannot do without `native/`; this entry point exposes
exactly the same `Scry.Prove.run` surface (`scry prove …`) so the corpus can be run
anywhere.

    scry-prove FILE --claim "noFlow Fixtures.Runner.Main"

The full CLI dispatches the same function: `scry prove FILE --claim …`.
-/
def main : IO Unit := IO.bind IO.args Scry.Prove.mainArgs
